# 0004. Plugins through tpm; sessions survive reboots without saving screen text

- Status: Proposed
- Date: 2026-11-19

tpm installs a small plugin set, and resurrect + continuum bring sessions back after a reboot,
but never write the text on screen to disk.

## Technical details
- **Plugin list in `tmux.conf`**: tpm finds plugins by reading the *text* of
  `~/.config/tmux/tmux.conf` and can't follow `source-file -F`. While the `@plugin` lines
  lived in `conf/plugins.conf`, nothing was ever installed or loaded (fixed in #1). A plugin
  listed anywhere else is silently ignored.
- **Plugins**: `tmux-plugins/tpm`, `tmux-resurrect`, `tmux-continuum`, `laktak/extrakto`
  (prefix Tab: fuzzy-pick a path / URL / word from the screen, copied via OSC 52).
- **Bootstrap** (`conf/plugins.conf`, loaded last so continuum can hook the status line):
  `TMUX_PLUGIN_MANAGER_PATH=~/.local/share/tmux/plugins`; tpm is cloned if missing, then
  `install_plugins` runs in the background on every start, because tpm only installs right
  after it is cloned. `make update` installs and updates all; `make clean` deletes them.
- **Sessions**: `@resurrect-dir ~/.local/share/tmux/resurrect`, `@continuum-save-interval 15`,
  `@continuum-restore on`; restarted programs: `lazygit btop k9s ssh "~uv run" "~go run"
  "~make run-server"`. Manual save / restore: `prefix C-s` / `prefix C-r`.
- **No screen text**: `@resurrect-capture-pane-contents off`. With it on, whatever was printed
  (`cat .env`, `env`, tokens) went to disk, unencrypted, every 15 minutes. Windows, panes,
  folders and programs are still restored; scrollback is not.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: tpm, tmux-resurrect, tmux-continuum, extrakto (needs python3, fzf).
- Alternatives: no plugin manager, vendored plugins (updates by hand, plugins in git);
  capturing pane contents (convenient, leaks secrets to disk).
